#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid ""
"You said you could tell me more about the shelter if I wanted.  How did "
"these things get built?"
msgstr ""
"Ты сказал, что можешь рассказать мне больше о бункере, если я захочу. Как "
"оно было построено?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid "You sure do."
msgstr "Точно."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid ""
"You think that's funny?!  Some of us watched the warning signs for years.  "
"All the news, all the violence and the secret plots…  Now the dead are "
"walking, reality itself is tearing apart, and you're making jokes like that?!"
msgstr ""
"Думаешь, это смешно?! Некоторые из нас годами видели предупреждающие знаки. "
"Все новости, всё насилие и тайные заговоры… Теперь мертвецы — ходячие, сама "
"реальность рвётся на части, а ты шутишь?!"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid ""
"You wouldn't keep ALL your tricks and secrets from me, though, would you?  "
"After everything we've been through?"
msgstr ""
"Ты ведь не стал бы скрывать от меня ВСЕ свои уловки и секреты, не так ли? "
"После всего, через что мы прошли."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgctxt "npc:f"
msgid ""
"You're not really a good liar.  I built that thing like a fortress.  No one "
"would just break into it."
msgstr ""
"Ври лучше. Я построила эту штуку на века. Просто так туда никто не вломится."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
